1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,754
One modern answer to the question, is simply math

2
00:00:03,854 --> 00:00:06,980
is the set of theorems of ZFC set theory.

3
00:00:07,133 --> 00:00:12,588
Where ZFC stands for Zermelo, Fraenkel plus Choice, and is axiomatized

4
00:00:12,688 --> 00:00:17,271
by these set of axioms. We will answer why these particular

5
00:00:17,371 --> 00:00:21,556
axioms later, but for now just know that these are the

6
00:00:21,656 --> 00:00:26,953
best attempt to formalize all of mathematics into a single language.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,614
The theory of ZFC is every logical consequence of

8
00:00:30,714 --> 00:00:33,798
these axioms, which we can think of as all

9
00:00:33,898 --> 00:00:37,892
outputs of a certain special theorem proving computer.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,846
So, we feed in the axioms, and it outputs the

11
00:00:41,946 --> 00:00:47,548
logical consequences of these axioms, which we call the theorems.

12
00:00:47,733 --> 00:00:50,627
Then we can feed these theorems back in as

13
00:00:50,727 --> 00:00:54,761
input, and we continue deriving new mathematical theorems.

14
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,254
So, there is some pre-existing space of all possible proofs

15
00:00:59,354 --> 00:01:03,093
from this set of axioms, and the goal of mathematics

16
00:01:03,193 --> 00:01:06,636
is to explore as much of this space as possible.

17
00:01:06,866 --> 00:01:09,672
There are multiple ways of formalizing what

18
00:01:09,772 --> 00:01:12,646
the inside of this theorem proving computer.

19
00:01:12,866 --> 00:01:17,677
Perhaps the simplest is with the so called Hilbert Calculus, which

20
00:01:17,777 --> 00:01:21,694
is just this set of axioms equipped with modus ponens.

21
00:01:21,866 --> 00:01:27,541
These axioms determine the behaviour of the logical negation, implication,

22
00:01:27,641 --> 00:01:31,677
and universal quantifier, and they turn out to be all

23
00:01:31,777 --> 00:01:35,110
that we need to formalize first order logic.

24
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:40,713
Modus ponens, can be seen as the application of a computer program,

25
00:01:40,813 --> 00:01:45,562
where phi implies psi means that it takes in phi and outputs

26
00:01:45,662 --> 00:01:48,956
psi, so if we then feed in phi we get psi.

27
00:01:49,133 --> 00:01:54,367
Not rocket science. But the necessary complexity comes from the fact

28
00:01:54,467 --> 00:01:58,681
that we can pass functions as input to other functions.

29
00:02:06,533 --> 00:02:10,221
So we can design or derive, complex interconnect

30
00:02:10,321 --> 00:02:14,089
circuits of logical variables using these axioms.

31
00:02:14,266 --> 00:02:18,280
And this set of axioms is of a special kind, since

32
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:23,627
it can only prove logically valid statements, and as Godel proved

33
00:02:23,727 --> 00:02:28,974
in 1929, it can prove all logically valid first order statements.

34
00:02:29,066 --> 00:02:33,433
So, we can think of these set of axioms, known as the

35
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:39,502
logical axioms, as the operating system of our theorem proving computer.

36
00:02:39,666 --> 00:02:43,464
Then we add in new symbols specific to our given theory

37
00:02:43,564 --> 00:02:48,071
to the language, add axioms controlling these symbols and we feed

38
00:02:48,171 --> 00:02:51,686
in new axioms to our theorem prover and let it run.

39
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,641
This view of mathematics aligns with the formalist view

40
00:02:55,741 --> 00:02:58,294
of math, namely that it is a game being

41
00:02:58,394 --> 00:03:02,172
played by meaningless symbols according to certain rules.

